{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02FW", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-dimension-at-a-point-preserved-field-extension}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-inequalities-under-field-extension}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0b68be60812b3d973188484fbb236cd485250e7c7865bc890738ced90a0d00bd", "source_text": "Part (1) follows immediately from\nAlgebra,\nLemma <REF_0001>.\nParts (2) and (3) from\nAlgebra, Lemma <REF_0002>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:d872a17e325d9ab0af195eebb4f5132f227fb586024120216cf653fcc8fb70e0", "unit_id": "tag:02FY:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "paragraph", "parent_tag": "02FW", "placeholders": {"STRUCT_0001": "\\noindent"}, "render": {"prefix": "", "suffix": ""}, "risk_level": "R2", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0c02473b83a395724968f95535a5ebfc74bcc9a33f7444ba2c8e741fa68037a3", "source_text": "\n\n<STRUCT_0001>\nThe following lemma follows from a nontrivial algebraic result.\nNamely, the algebraic version of Zariski's main theorem.\n\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:2728998b605f45db31fbb297ebe0368f3e1eaaf35bd7101ad50f64f7077dfbc1", "unit_id": "tag:02FW:prose-0002"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02FW", "placeholders": {"LOCKED_0001": "\\begin{reference}\n\\cite[IV Theorem 13.1.3]{EGA}\n\\end{reference}", "MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$n \\geq 0$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nU_n = \\{x \\in X \\mid \\dim_x X_{f(x)} \\leq n\\}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$X$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-openness-bounded-dimension-fibres}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5e8e6955b0e4c9ddcac35fd9939441218ca1464833639d38a79eff2054e59de9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:d621a1d0f26ff8c5c764099d59c0dae9646cac071090e03e615b6576a799032b", "source_text": "<LOCKED_0001>\nLet <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002>. Assume <MATH_0003> is locally of finite type.\nThe set\n<MATH_0004>\nis open in <MATH_0005>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:c2a28cad7d3c62c306441a85a2945f826dfe9f3652352f4e86bacf0f084bf85a", "unit_id": "tag:02FZ:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02FW", "placeholders": {"REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-dimension-fibres-bounded-open-upstairs}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:44136fa355b3678a1146ad16f7e8649e94fb4fc21fe77e8310c060f61caaff8a", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:dadf345a3225a655e5155a7fab994cea90550d6fec54acb80ac4097fa40fc34a", "source_text": "This is immediate from\nAlgebra,\nLemma <REF_0001>\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:8def8621d0cb21bff4dba890a650446fb99167c0fc1b6866e50271197aafd6ce", "unit_id": "tag:02FZ:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02FW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to Y$", "MATH_0002": "$Y$", "MATH_0003": "$f$"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-morphism-finite-type-bounded-dimension}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:625bff47b0e60986364523d5a9aeabc74372b53ecb6c3e444062d88cbe7eec96", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:e447b41964f3ae57ba4f421b11598c0b8c5485a250621adb475cdb680d8c9311", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of finite type with <MATH_0002> quasi-compact.\nThen the dimension of the fibres of <MATH_0003> is bounded.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:4b001412fe3b8e2d6ac29371994cf731d0204ac30a80256810b4035ab4490953", "unit_id": "tag:0A3V:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02FW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$U_n \\subset X$", "MATH_0002": "$\\leq n$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$U_n$", "MATH_0005": "$Y$", "MATH_0006": "$f$", "MATH_0007": "$X$", "MATH_0008": "$X = U_n$", "MATH_0009": "$n$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-openness-bounded-dimension-fibres}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:3cafb78fad79a4d09b2b708d1d815c658e9dd0eef82236b689ce22a8b9ce050e", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:cfa20552cad192e05ee2b7d32475ef65a27eb22ba27f36289ed4225db72f02da", "source_text": "By Lemma <REF_0001>\nthe set <MATH_0001> of points where the dimension of the fibre\nis <MATH_0002> is open. Since <MATH_0003> is of finite type, every point is\ncontained in some <MATH_0004> (because the dimension of a finite\ntype algebra over a field is finite). Since <MATH_0005> is quasi-compact and <MATH_0006> is of\nfinite type, we see that <MATH_0007> is quasi-compact. Hence <MATH_0008> for\nsome <MATH_0009>.\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:25ab3b11606cc64b1c1a3e274429aa53ec3b074136844becc8d53ae40050fc1d", "unit_id": "tag:0A3V:proof"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "lemma", "parent_tag": "02FW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$f : X \\to S$", "MATH_0002": "$n \\geq 0$", "MATH_0003": "$f$", "MATH_0004": "$$\nU_n = \\{x \\in X \\mid \\dim_x X_{f(x)} \\leq n\\}\n$$", "MATH_0005": "$X$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{lemma-openness-bounded-dimension-fibres}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{topology-definition-quasi-compact}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{lemma}\n\\label{lemma-openness-bounded-dimension-fibres-finite-presentation}\n", "suffix": "\\end{lemma}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:5e8e6955b0e4c9ddcac35fd9939441218ca1464833639d38a79eff2054e59de9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:0fdc7a6551e651650a4e6905191567026d5bc7e57b8781db2150d127af27b75f", "source_text": "Let <MATH_0001> be a morphism of schemes.\nLet <MATH_0002>. Assume <MATH_0003> is locally of finite presentation.\nThe open\n<MATH_0004>\nof Lemma <REF_0001> is retrocompact\nin <MATH_0005>. (See Topology, Definition <REF_0002>.)\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:0b72295fc771c155b26a5c6f669ec5bf0e9a7b0792fe4756a65928e8894e0936", "unit_id": "tag:02G0:statement"}
{"chapter": "morphisms", "node_kind": "proof", "parent_tag": "02FW", "placeholders": {"MATH_0001": "$X$", "MATH_0002": "$U \\subset X$", "MATH_0003": "$f|_U : U \\to S$", "MATH_0004": "$V \\subset S$", "MATH_0005": "$U \\cap U_n$", "MATH_0006": "$U$", "MATH_0007": "$U_n \\cap U$", "MATH_0008": "$\\{x \\in U \\mid \\dim_x U_{f(x)} \\leq n\\}$", "MATH_0009": "$X$", "MATH_0010": "$S$", "REF_0001": "\\ref{algebra-lemma-dimension-fibres-bounded-quasi-compact-open-upstairs}", "REF_0002": "\\ref{lemma-locally-finite-presentation-characterize}"}, "render": {"prefix": "\\begin{proof}\n", "suffix": "\\end{proof}"}, "risk_level": "R3", "schema_version": 1, "source_commit": "a04446e57ec1fbc252a871afcec7752fb2807b14", "source_math_hash": "sha256:45ae071daa56f8ecf646c0147aad3b06805bc1c0ed6d365ce8b0febb05a20fc9", "source_status": "CURRENT", "source_structure_hash": "sha256:f0f71e9f2b86b3383ea99ad7a676a7514cbbbbfa3b52b5b04557210b14e30671", "source_text": "The topological space <MATH_0001> has a basis for its topology consisting of\naffine opens <MATH_0002> such that the induced morphism\n<MATH_0003> factors through an affine open <MATH_0004>. Hence\nit is enough to show that <MATH_0005> is quasi-compact for such a <MATH_0006>.\nNote that <MATH_0007> is the same as the open\n<MATH_0008>. This reduces us to the case\nwhere <MATH_0009> and <MATH_0010> are affine. In this case the lemma follows from\nAlgebra,\nLemma <REF_0001>\n(and Lemma <REF_0002>).\n", "source_text_hash": "sha256:3d7d6fd0e6c12a8c9656410f37a5a012da6de49d7c29b79419498b0559f36e84", "unit_id": "tag:02G0:proof"}
